{
  "_note": "Success floors for the load test (bench/load). floors holds, per pod shape and scenario, the fewest successes the scenario may have in its loaded pass and, where it joins that pass, in its concurrency-one pass. A run held to the floors fails on a count below its floor, on a scenario without a floor, and on a floor that names no scenario. A ramp holds every step to its floor, and a paired scenario both of its loads. A run is held only when it matches calibration: on GitHub Actions under runnerOs and runnerArch, at operatingPoint, under a pod shape that floors holds, and while its npm fixture injects at most npmInjectedLatency.ceilingMs of upstream latency. In operatingPoint, null leaves a bound to the proxy's computed default, null scenarios means every scenario, and patternOverrides names the BENCH_PATTERN_* variables set. runs lists every run a floor came from, each with the commit it measured. npmInjectedLatency.highestMs holds, per pod shape, the highest upstream latency the npm fixture injected in those runs. docs/testing.md, Success floors, has the recalibration procedure.",
